Thanks Finn,

Just to be clear, my issue is no longer that the INLAutils tests fail on the CRAN solaris servers etc. That did use to be an issue (moving targets) but now it is simply the principle of relying on INLA with INLA not being on CRAN.

"if they agree to having the documentation examples disabled for running actual inla code that might be ok."

I can't see why they would disagree with this. Any packages with APIs have most of their examples in \dontrun{} for example.

"The other main issue has historically been the rapid update-cycle of INLA"

It seems that a rapid update cycle for the dev version available from the INLA site and a slower update cycle for the CRAN version is a good compromise here.

In general, let me know if there is anything I can do to help (bearing in mind I don't know c++).

Tim

