> CRAN.

Yes, I was just referring to the potential issues involved in getting
INLA onto CRAN.

> "if they agree to having the documentation examples disabled for running
> actual inla code that might be ok."
> I can't see why they would disagree with this. Any packages with APIs have
> most of their examples in \dontrun{} for example.

In the past, they did have an issue with this, but they have evolved.

> "The other main issue has historically been the rapid update-cycle of INLA"
> It seems that a rapid update cycle for the dev version available from the
> INLA site and a slower update cycle for the CRAN version is a good
> compromise here.

I agree.

> In general, let me know if there is anything I can do to help (bearing in
> mind I don't know c++).

inla itself is plain C, but knowledge of Makefile's and how to make
CRAN happy about them is probably the most important puzzle.
fmesher is C++, but there I have a better grasp of the issues, as I've
been slowly preparing to split the fmesher parts of INLA into a
separate package to put on CRAN.

Finn

