>>>> is becoming the center of an ecosystem rather than a simple standalone
>>>> package. Thinking long term about how best to distribute INLA and related
>>>> packages would benefit everyone (and in that I acknowledge that your careers
>>>> etc. may be your prime concern). If CRAN is not an option then perhaps you
>>>> could think about hosting packages that depend on CRAN somewhere alongside
>>>> it, as suggested in the email from CRAN. Or something. Or perhaps an
>>>> actively maintained list of packages that use INLA is the easiest first step
>>>> (which I will try to get around to doing myself).
>>>>
>>>> I hope I don't come across as demanding of your time or effort. And
>>>> thanks again for your work.
>>>>
>>>> Tim
